# Extracted loop value keeps the subtype it was loaded with

Verifies `let x = a[0]` is a value, not a location. The body loads `x` before
rewriting `a[0]`, so the first iteration prints `10mm + 1mm = 11mm` while the
second loads the stored centimeter value and prints `21mm`.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]

for (i in 0..2) {
    let x = a[0]
    a[0] = 2cm
    print(x + 1mm)
}

<<< stdout
11mm
21mm

<<< stderr
